<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmedi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1334–1413</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmedi was an Anatolian Turkish poet who wrote at the courts of the Germiyanid beys and later of the Ottoman prince Süleyman Çelebi. His İskendername, a long verse romance on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a>, includes a section on Ottoman history that is among the earliest Ottoman chronicles. He was one of the founders of Ottoman Turkish literature.</p></div>
